1
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:10,940
What's wrong?

2
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,500
I'm nervous, man. My first day at work.

3
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,840
But I think I should've dropped you off.

4
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,580
It's fine. It's far, you'd just be driving back and forth.

5
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:23,700
Wow.

6
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,420
When it was Phrae-Bangkok, you could drive back and forth just fine.

7
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,680
Can't I do it sometimes?

8
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,820
You've grown up, yet you're so stubborn.

9
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,120
You know?

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,340
Don't use the words 'grown up' with me.

11
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,600
Don't act too cute, alright?

12
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,340
If I end up not wanting to work,

13
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:42,220
what are you going to do?

14
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,540
Besides, I already rejected your company.

15
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:47,820
I have nowhere else to go now.

16
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:51,060
You brought this on yourself.

17
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,100
Then next time, can you invite P'Ton and the guys over?

18
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,180
I miss them.

19
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,540
Can I think about it first?

20
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,820
Hey, why?

21
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:03,580
Yeah, just saying.

22
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,060
Alright, go.

23
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:07,460
You can go now.

24
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,140
Go on.

25
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:09,300
You're acting weird.

26
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,980
It's your first day of work. You'll be late.

27
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:14,920
EP15 The Future

28
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:23,700
Hmph.

29
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:25,480
P'Dan.

30
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,360
P'Dan's boy...

31
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:29,420
is working on the other side?

32
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,380
Who do you mean, Jay?

33
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:35,220
Pond?

34
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:35,920
Yeah.

35
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:38,880
Here it is.

36
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:40,280
"First love...

37
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,360
and first day at work."

38
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,660
"First love and first day at work."

39
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:46,820
Such a super sweet message.

40
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,040
Weird. / What?

41
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,540
First love?

42
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,040
Who is the first love?

43
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,220
Nobody.

44
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:07,160
Sigh...

45
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:09,320
If we didn't know, P'Dan probably wouldn't know either, I think.

46
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,100
But P'Dan...

47
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,360
liked every single photo.

48
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:18,040
I just hit like.

49
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:19,880
I hit like on everyone's posts.

50
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,080
But do you 'Love' him?

51
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,600
Just giving encouragement, things like that.

52
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,560
See?

53
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:32,920
Nobody will blame you if you get back together with your ex.

54
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,460
We'd be happy for you.

55
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,440
But is it possible?

56
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:43,120
He went out of his way to work on the other side,

57
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,900
just so he could come back to this side,

58
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,340
and then go to the other side,

59
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:47,860
to pick him up on this side.

60
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:48,500
Oh...

61
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,220
Isn't that a bit too dedicated?

62
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,620
Yeah, who would be that dedicated?

63
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:57,660
I think there is someone.

64
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,420
No way.

65
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:01,680
Probably someone around here.

66
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:05,480
Nobody.

67
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,340
You're acting suspicious again.

68
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:09,080
I'm not doing anything.

69
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:11,080
I'm just stiff, so I'm stretching.

70
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:14,320
You see, I watch a lot of Korean series. Korean male leads love to act like this.

71
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,440
You're suspicious.

72
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:19,080
I'm not.

73
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:21,580
I'm not. / I'm just stiff.

74
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,240
You're really not?

75
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,640
Right.

76
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:35,860
Smells good?

77
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,660
Well...

78
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:39,620
it's good.

79
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:43,940
Just good?

80
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:45,060
Just that?

81
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,080
We are dating, instead of saying nice things...

82
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:50,360
the listener wants to feel good too.

83
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,700
It smells good.

84
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:55,280
Smells really good. Satisfied yet?

85
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,400
Want me to teach you?

86
00:05:00,620 --> 00:05:02,620
Just in case I get off work late someday,

87
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,500
you can cook for yourself.

88
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:08,440
I can just order food.

89
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,200
After work, I'd want a boyfriend...

90
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,240
to have food waiting for me.

91
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,580
Can't I have that?

92
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,080
Then...

93
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:24,780
can I wait to do something else?

94
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:45,860
In the kitchen isn't bad either, P'.

95
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:52,480
I'm just kidding.

96
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:05,200
Hey... that's enough.

97
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:13,040
P'Dan.

98
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:15,320
Where are you, P'?

99
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:17,020
P'Dan.

100
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,460
Surprise! Hey...

101
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:21,640
Pond.

102
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,540
What are you doing, P'Dan?

103
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:26,600
Uh...

104
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,140
Now I know...

105
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,520
what kind of crazy person takes a ride from one side...

106
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,260
to work on the other side.

107
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,220
Isn't that a bit too much effort, P'Dan?

108
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,760
You sold your condo to live with Ton, and I didn't say a single word.

109
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,620
Really?

110
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:48,420
Don't talk about my P'Best like that.

111
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:49,640
Yeah.

112
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:51,720
Then why didn't you guys tell us...

113
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,060
that you're living together?

114
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,840
I'm always with P'Dan anyway.

115
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,480
Didn't P'Dan tell you guys?

116
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:01,660
I... was afraid of getting teased.

117
00:07:02,100 --> 00:07:03,240
I'd definitely tease you.

118
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:05,120
Especially since I found out later like this...

119
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,360
I'm going to tease you. I'm going to tell everyone in the office...

120
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,780
that you guys are living together.

121
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:09,980
Good.

122
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,460
I'll help boost the ads too.

123
00:07:11,460 --> 00:07:13,700
Hey... bring it on! Media team needs to step up.

124
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,120
Don't do that.

125
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,380
I was wondering...

126
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,880
why you were working so hard.

127
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,560
Working like a heartbroken person, P'Dan.

128
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,900
I just... didn't want to think about him too much.

129
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,060
Wow...

130
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:29,280
So romantic.

131
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,820
Yeah, you refused to go anywhere we invited you.

132
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:33,420
I thought you had a new girlfriend in your room.

133
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:34,560
But it turns out...

134
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:36,480
you two were secretly living together.

135
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,960
I just wanted to be... sure first.

136
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:45,020
What's not to be sure about? Wow... living together like this...

137
00:07:45,020 --> 00:07:46,940
soon you guys will be signing a marriage certificate.

138
00:07:46,940 --> 00:07:47,520
Yeah.

139
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:48,980
Just like you two.

140
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,400
Don't tease us.

141
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:54,500
I'm currently mad at you guys.

142
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,560
But it's good that you two...

143
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,920
successfully got together.

144
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,400
You've secretly liked him for a long time anyway.

145
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,800
A really long time, P'.

146
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,780
Not you, P'Dan...

147
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:10,760
has liked Pond for a long time, hasn't he?

148
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:12,320
Shut up, Best.

149
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,620
You've had a crush on him since his first day at work,

150
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:15,860
and I didn't say a thing.

151
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,340
You've secretly liked me since the first day?

152
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:19,420
Then why didn't you tell me?

153
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:21,200
Letting me flirt with you for so long.

154
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:22,800
Cost me a lot of money.

155
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:24,480
He just wanted to play hard to get.

156
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,700
Just like you.

157
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:27,200
I wasn't playing.

158
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,500
Tonight, P'...

159
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,100
we have a lot to clear up.

160
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,420
For many rounds.

161
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,220
Why would you say that?

162
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,460
Well, you didn't tell me.

163
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,280
Right...

164
00:08:45,280 --> 00:08:45,900
we're heading back now.

165
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,580
You guys...

166
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:47,300
clear it up yourselves.

167
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:48,000
Yeah.

168
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,720
I'm going to play for many rounds too.

169
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:52,000
I won't let you outdo me.

170
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:05,860
Here he is, P'Dan.

171
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,140
Hello, Jay.

172
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:11,340
Oh... Pond, how have you been?

173
00:09:11,340 --> 00:09:13,220
I'm good. How about you, Jay?

174
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,940
I'm fine. Oh...

175
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:17,200
Wait a minute, you're working on the other side.

176
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,340
Are you here to steal my data or something?

177
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:21,720
Someone at my level wouldn't steal your work.

178
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:23,700
Stealing his heart is enough.

179
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,740
Wow...

180
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,080
I'm sorry.

181
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,900
Suddenly, I feel...

182
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:33,020
inexplicably nauseous.

183
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,800
Sigh... Working on this side...

184
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,560
but picking up and dropping off on the other side.

185
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:40,240
No wonder some people are...

186
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,720
so crazy about this younger boy.

187
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:45,460
Because you talk like this, who would tell you?

188
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:48,780
What about you two? You said you'd stay 2 meters apart.

189
00:09:48,780 --> 00:09:50,260
Then why are you sticking together like this?

190
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:51,600
Your info is inaccurate again.

191
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,320
It's 1 meter and 15 centimeters.

192
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:56,760
And now, they've moved even closer together.

193
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:00,800
Listening to this makes my knees weak.

194
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:04,040
Jay, what's wrong with you?

195
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:07,480
Low calcium? Or are you just getting old?

196
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,820
That's a bit harsh, isn't it? Might as well call her an old hag.

197
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:13,060
Can I say that? Can I actually say that?

198
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,600
Enough.

199
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,240
That's enough.

200
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,660
Since everyone is here...

201
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:22,060
Actually...

202
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:25,240
I have something I want to tell everyone.

203
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:27,140
Go ahead and tell them.

204
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:30,260
What is it? / Hmm?

205
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:31,380
I'm in suspense here.

206
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,720
The two of us...

207
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,580
are going to live together.

208
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:39,940
Ooh! / Really?

209
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:42,180
Does this mean you two...

210
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:43,820
are getting married?

211
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:45,500
I think so, P'.

212
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,060
Hey... do I need to get a groomsman suit tailored?

213
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:54,740
I'm tearing up. I've raised you since you were babies.

214
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:56,540
Are you really getting married?

215
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:57,460
Yes.

216
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,080
Congratulations.

217
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,920
Besides the congratulations...

218
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:03,480
I have something I need everyone's help with.

219
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,100
What?

220
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:09,940
Here it is.

221
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:11,060
The QR Code.

222
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:13,360
From your best friends.

223
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:16,380
Department Head... right here.

224
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,580
"Raised you since..."

225
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,120
"...since you were babies", right?

226
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,940
Here it is.

227
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:24,160
I don't know where my hands are right now.

228
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,980
Mine is kept with P'Dan.

229
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:28,200
Friend.

230
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,740
Alright... come on... kick it off.

231
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,280
How much? How much, you decide.

232
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:34,560
Go ahead.

233
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:39,180
Set a good example. Watch closely, guys.

234
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:42,680
Okay, I have to go follow up on the boss's stuff first.

235
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:01,220
P'Ton looks happy, doesn't he?

236
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,460
Well, he's getting married.

237
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:08,380
Don't you want to get married?

238
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:12,420
Do you know how many hurdles they had to overcome to get married?

239
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:15,060
And how many hurdles do I have to overcome?

240
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:19,920
Just because you see your friends getting married doesn't mean you have to follow suit.

241
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,740
Then I'll wait for the day you're ready.

242
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:25,900
Then I'll get married.

243
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:29,420
But honestly...

244
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:31,640
I'm waiting for you to propose to me too.

245
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:33,300
That would be so satisfying.

246
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:41,340
What are you smiling at?

247
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,080
Nothing.

248
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:46,840
I just...

249
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:52,180
didn't think I'd have the chance to be in your future for that long.

250
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,320
My future...

251
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:58,220
has you in every part of it.

252
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:11,480
Pond.

253
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,080
If I... told you that...

254
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,700
I haven't thought that far ahead yet...

255
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,040
would you be mad at me?

256
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:23,400
I'm not you.

257
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,060
But if you haven't started thinking about anything yet...

258
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:33,080
then should we start thinking about it together?

259
00:13:35,700 --> 00:13:37,100
Starting from...

260
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:44,440
Wait.

261
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,720
Let me start first.

262
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:11,220
I can't take it.

263
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:14,640
Hey.

264
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:19,180
You can't do that.

265
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:20,600
You have to take it.

266
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,440
If you can't...

267
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:25,580
I'll start myself.

268
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:02,600
Share your thoughts on the series "New Boyfriend".

269
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:05,080
Comment your impressions under this video,

270
